00:24:52.040 --> 00:24:54.540
And then you two, you know, I'd say I'd pull you apart.
然后你们两个，你知道，我会说我要把你们拆开。

569
00:24:55.100 --> 00:24:57.780
Start to think about something about Jim that you didn't like.
开始想一些你不喜欢的关于吉姆的事情。

570
00:24:58.520 --> 00:24:58.760
Yeah.
是啊。

571
00:24:59.360 --> 00:25:01.280
Just throw a wrench into everything.
简直是给一切捣乱。

572
00:25:01.480 --> 00:25:04.640
He's like, I don't think this – so there's nothing – a director.
他会说，我不觉得这——所以没什么——导演。

573
00:25:04.640 --> 00:25:13.720
A director on episodic television just comes in and tries to – what my whole goal was whenever I direct television,
电视剧的导演只是过来尝试——我每次执导电视剧的全部目标就是，

574
00:25:14.020 --> 00:25:22.700
which is different from directing features because in features it's – you are trying and need to please yourself.
这和执导电影不同，因为在电影里——你是在尝试并需要取悦你自己。

575
00:25:22.700 --> 00:25:29.140
And make sure that you get all those elements and moments that you've worked so hard in breaking down that script.
并确保你得到了所有你在拆解剧本时辛苦准备的那些元素和瞬间。

576
00:25:29.400 --> 00:25:39.100
In television, it's about staying true to these characters, putting them in positions where they can really be themselves, where they feel comfortable.
在电视里，关键在于忠于这些角色，把他们放在能让他们真正做自己的位置，让他们感到舒适。

577
00:25:39.100 --> 00:25:45.280
It's delivering the meat and potatoes that every showrunner is going to expect from you.
关键是提供每一位剧集主管所期望的“家常便饭”。

578
00:25:45.480 --> 00:25:55.340
I always thought if I can deliver two or three things that the showrunner didn't see, that's golden.
我一直认为，如果我能提供两三样剧集主管没想到的东西，那就太棒了。

579
00:25:55.340 --> 00:25:58.120
Just a couple little things.
就那么几个小点子。

580
00:25:58.120 --> 00:25:59.760
I think there's a few.
我觉得有几个。

581
00:25:59.960 --> 00:26:05.680
